HyperFrames

CupriLex translates compositions written for HyperFrames, and its test corpus is
the HyperFrames registry:

    https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes
    Copyright HeyGen
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The corpus is NOT redistributed in this repository. tools/fetch-corpus.py pulls
it on demand into corpus/, which is git-ignored.

A composition translated by this tool should record which block it came from -
not because the Apache licence requires a notice in a rendered video, but
because a project that cannot say where its design came from is one nobody can
re-license later.
